From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GammaOS's stereo_skip and async_gpu_flush_lag as core options

Patch 013 turned the two switches on for Castlevania: Lords of Shadow -
Mirror of Fate by its title ID, and the core read them once. Now they are
core options under Graphics, so a game the list does not know can have them
too, and one it knows can have them off:

- Interleaved Right Eye Skip (citra_stereo_skip): Auto, Enabled, Disabled.
- GPU Flush Lag (citra_gpu_flush_lag): Auto, Off, 8, 16, 24, 32, 64 jobs.

Auto, the default, takes the title's value from title_switches in
core_settings.cpp (Castlevania: the skip and a lag of 24) and leaves every
other game to the property, that is the environment variable of patch 002,
unset and so off, as GammaOS has them. A set environment variable still wins
over the list at Auto.

The renderer and the GPU read the values (Settings::values, -1 for "the
property decides") at every display transfer and cache flush instead of once,
so a change in the menu applies at once; turning the skip off forgets the
right eye target it learned, which is then drawn and copied again.

